    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. I haven't run or tested it, as instructed.\n\n- **Storage:** each client has its own queue of `(time, cost)` entries. Entries that are `window_seconds` old or older are dropped before any calculation.\n- **`allow`:** it records the request only if the units in use plus `cost` fit within `limit`. A rejected request records nothing.\n- **`remaining` and `retry_after`:** neither records anything. `retry_after` returns `0.0` if the request would fit now. Otherwise it expires the oldest entries one at a time until the cost fits, and returns the seconds from `now` until that entry expires.\n- **Validation:**\n  - `limit`, `window_seconds` and `cost` are checked as the spec requires, and `bool` is rejected for the integer ones.\n  - `ValueError` is raised if `now` is lower than the highest time seen across all clients. Equal times are accepted.\n  - I check `cost` before the time, so a call with an invalid `cost` does not move the latest-time marker.\n\nThe spec doesn't say whether `remaining` should reject a `now` that goes backwards. I applied the time check to every method, as rule 8 says \"any method\".",
